{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[{"claim_ids":["clm_91e5e63fffac48e7fe134d3adc566f1fab75e4dd5b0379bfe7b584205d5d4a65"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Repository development practice: the docs subdirectory is a Next.js/Fumadocs application; its README describes starting a dev server via npm run dev, pnpm dev, or yarn dev on localhost:3000."}],"claim_ids":["clm_91e5e63fffac48e7fe134d3adc566f1fab75e4dd5b0379bfe7b584205d5d4a65"],"created_at":"2026-09-14T02:29:01Z","created_by_operation":"op_55378d89afad4942854afbfc9836d5c8","id":"pg_32635de96c9f5430a09bb0b42f410050","maturity":"draft","page_type":"source","path":"pages/sources/pacifio-cersei-docs-readme-md-708c5055845b-b0b42f410050.md","record_type":"page","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","source_ids":["src_d27d95ac6f3158e0b671eae346097bf5"],"title":"pacifio/cersei/docs/README.md @ 708c5055845b","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:29:01Z","updated_by_operation":"op_55378d89afad4942854afbfc9836d5c8"}
{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[{"claim_ids":["clm_06f4228bb952599dbd759e294fcf575aad6e909b9e285be969fba93d634a9a21"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"MCP integration connects stdio and SSE servers via McpManager and exposes their tool definitions to the agent builder; the MCP client uses JSON-RPC 2.0 over stdio transport."},{"claim_ids":["clm_259d5738952c044e6d62eb05076b3cb496f5f5074538b22c426de2e9939724d6"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Skills auto-discover from .claude/commands/*.md, .claude/skills/*/SKILL.md, user-level ~/.claude/commands, and bundled skills; a SkillTool lists skills and expands $ARGUMENTS templates."},{"claim_ids":["clm_51939f3e0ab35c2240d6fbd7ca403c16c7400d8aa61742866f5d9de88b95365c"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Repository development practice: the README instructs running the workspace test suite with 'cargo test --workspace', optionally with '--features graph', or per-crate with 'cargo test -p cersei-tools' and similar."},{"claim_ids":["clm_6c5954b537d41eb74d6d9fae0c51a418d72da816264d745e43ded2facae57883"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Using the SDK requires adding cersei (via git), tokio with the 'full' feature, and anyhow; the #[derive(Tool)] macro additionally needs async-trait and a cersei-tools dependency."},{"claim_ids":["clm_7c7b381fa6f40cdf53fb0762e308f25144a875960519f212a18e78b787a2873d"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Sessions persist as append-only JSONL with tombstone soft-delete, and messages can be written and reloaded per session id."},{"claim_ids":["clm_99c766990a956f80d84f6e9a94579da166d052fe3c0f83715ed932e8bc0e1f96"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Memory is three-tier: flat markdown files scanned with frontmatter, a CLAUDE.md hierarchy merged into context, and an optional Grafeo graph layer supporting tagged store/recall queries with text fallback."},{"claim_ids":["clm_9a43e031744baf7f41efecd557529d3510fe04ef902fa22b76dd03a752d11c6b"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The SDK exposes a runtime permission model with selectable policies including AllowAll, AllowReadOnly, DenyAll, RuleBased, and Interactive, plus interactive permissions with session caching in the CLI."},{"claim_ids":["clm_a21cb760f77cdf377656f6df7fb6c870c2a5ac597fc0e9ee5735a8837521aa16"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The workspace is organized into crates including cersei-types, cersei-provider, cersei-tools, cersei-tools-derive, cersei-agent, cersei-memory, cersei-hooks, cersei-mcp, a cersei facade crate, and abstract-cli."},{"claim_ids":["clm_a2c4be17e1ec17fd42aec0f2457c1802da1b4606e364f6a1a9ad8b0374109dfb"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Cersei is described as a Rust SDK exposing the building blocks of a coding agent — tool execution, LLM streaming, sub-agent orchestration, persistent memory, skills, and MCP integration — as composable library functions."},{"claim_ids":["clm_b059bd89bafae3c4faf876bae440748168ab533584db7412cc64054d43773065"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The repo ships agent-performance benchmarks: Terminal Bench 2.0 end-to-end coding tasks in Daytona sandboxes, LongMemEval recall accuracy vs Mastra/Zep/Supermemory with LLM-as-judge, and general-agent framework comparisons."},{"claim_ids":["clm_f8fa920e10027f871240ab9bc5cfcdf64ba8763a63c7b89c23d9523498455dc1"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Agents are constructed via a builder API supporting provider, tools, model/temperature/max_tokens, system prompt, working directory, permission policy, memory, hooks, and context-management options."},{"claim_ids":["clm_fce70803312adb0ffbb1d477af132890972a30ef4725ca58b2ad07c16f118bfd"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Sub-agent orchestration includes an AgentTool the model can spawn autonomously, a coordinator mode with parallel workers whose tools are filtered to prevent recursion, and a task system (TaskCreate through TaskOutput)."}],"claim_ids":["clm_06f4228bb952599dbd759e294fcf575aad6e909b9e285be969fba93d634a9a21","clm_259d5738952c044e6d62eb05076b3cb496f5f5074538b22c426de2e9939724d6","